Chapter: ChessAi
  cites Games chapter Chess

 Square indices: a8 = 0, f8 = 5, g8 = 6, h8 = 7, f7 = 13, g7 = 14,
 h7 = 15, a1 = 56, h1 = 63.

 The AI is graded on DECIDABLE tactics rather than on strength. A win rate
 or a self-play score would agree with an engine that had no search at all,
 which is the bar GAME-13 records; a mate in one either is found or is not.

 We say:

Section: Boards

  place-many : List Integer, List Integer, Integer -> ChessBoard
  place-many (sqs) (codes) (side) =
    let b = cs-place-loop chess-blank sqs codes (list-length sqs) 0
    in chess-to-move b side

  cs-place-loop : ChessBoard, List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> ChessBoard
  cs-place-loop (b) (sqs) (codes) (n) (i) =
    if i >= n then b
    else let b2 = chess-place b (list-at sqs i) (list-at codes i)
    in cs-place-loop b2 sqs codes n (i + 1)

 Black king g8 boxed in by its own pawns on f7, g7 and h7, white rook a1 and
 white king h1. Ra8 is mate: the rook checks along the eighth rank, f8 and h8
 are on that rank, and the three pawns are the king's own.

  mate-board : ChessBoard
  mate-board = place-many [6, 13, 14, 15, 56, 63] [12, 7, 7, 7, 4, 6] 0

 A black queen on a8 with nothing defending it, against a white rook that
 can take it. Any move but the capture leaves 900 centipawns on the board.

  hang-board : ChessBoard
  hang-board = place-many [0, 7, 56, 63] [11, 12, 4, 6] 0

Section: The Tactics

  ai-lines : [Console] Nothing
  ai-lines =
    let mb = mate-board
    in let before = format-chess-board mb
    in let mi = chess-best-move mb 2
    in let mm = list-at (chess-legal mb) mi
    in let after = format-chess-board mb
    in let played = chess-apply mb mm
    in let hb = hang-board
    in let hi = chess-best-move hb 2
    in let hm = list-at (chess-legal hb) hi
    in act
      print-line-uni ("mate in one: from " & show (mm.from-sq) & " to " & show (mm.to-sq))
      print-line-uni ("and it is mate " & (if chess-checkmate played then "yes" else "no"))
      print-line-uni ("the search left the board alone " & (if before == after then "yes" else "no"))
      print-line-uni ("free queen: from " & show (hm.from-sq) & " to " & show (hm.to-sq) & " captured " & show (hm.captured))
      print-line-uni ("white material before " & show (chess-material hb 0))
      print-line-uni ("white material after " & show (chess-material (chess-apply hb hm) 0))
    end

Section: The Evaluation Itself

  eval-lines : [Console] Nothing
  eval-lines =
    let start = chess-new
    in act
      print-line-uni ("start material, white " & show (chess-material start 0))
      print-line-uni ("start material, black " & show (chess-material start 1))
      print-line-uni ("a rook is worth five pawns " & (if cs-piece-value 4 == 5 * cs-piece-value 1 then "yes" else "no"))
      print-line-uni ("the king carries no material " & show (cs-piece-value 6))
    end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    ai-lines
    eval-lines
  end

